## Task
{{ arrivals_text }} {{ entered }} entered the room or location known as {{ room.name }}.

Your job is to describe what {{ arrivals_text }} can see on arriving in the location or room they just entered, not the one they left: what {{ room.name }} looks like right now.

Only describe what can be seen at this very moment. Do not reveal anything that was said or happened before {{ arrivals_text }} arrived, nor what anyone thinks or feels beyond visible expressions, nor anything {{ arrivals_text }} could not know by looking. Do not write any actions or dialogue for {{ arrivals_text }}.

Write it as narration in the present tense, at most {{ response_length }} tokens.

Do not include characters in this location unless they are in the room / location known as {{ room.name }} as well. The current locations of all characters in the story are:

{% for location in locations -%}
- {{ location.room.name }}: {% if location.characters %}{% for character in location.characters %}{{ character.name }}{% if character.unnoticed %}{% if location.room.id == room.id %} (hiding here unnoticed, {{ arrivals_text }} cannot see them, do not describe them){% else %} (unnoticed by the others there){% endif %}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% else %}no one{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if present -%}
At the moment, {{ present_text }} {{ "are" if present|length > 1 else "is" }} shown in the location list above as being already present in {{ room.name }} when {{ arrivals_text }} entered the room / location known as {{ room.name }}.
{%- else -%}
At the moment, none of the characters in the location list above are in the room / location known as {{ room.name }}.
